import STFSpec.Hash

/-!
# SHA-256 production digest regressions

Library `EthConformance`.
Spec guidance: `STFSpec/informal/modules/EthHash.md` §§3, 4.

## References

Primary vectors: NIST CAVP CAVS 11.0 `SHA256ShortMsg.rsp`, Len 0/440/448/512:
NIST CAVP byte-oriented SHA vectors (`shabytetestvectors.zip`):
https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-algorithm-validation-program/secure-hashing
The abc digest is NIST's SHA256 worked example (page 3):
NIST SHA256 worked example (`SHA256.pdf`):
https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-standards-and-guidelines/example-values
Only the selected message/digest facts are transcribed, not the archive or paper.
Conceptual huge lengths below exercise the Q46 helper, never a huge ByteArray.
-/

